WEBVTT

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.690
All begins and ends.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:11.570
Within that cycle was I born,
unlooked for.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.610
Who am I?

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.490
As of today, you're James Tyrrell.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.990
Bring everyone salvation.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.000
Where is James Tyrrell?

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.710
Tyrrell's a shepherd, sir.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:31.510
We only give him room
and board for his work.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.550
Then tell the shepherd this:

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:38.220
The future King Richard is his new master.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.850
The living are punished.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.400
We live today that we might perish.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.650
York of the white rose.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.280
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:02.700
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:07.460
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:43.930
Are you cold?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.850
I'm fine as long as I have wine.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.890
But this tastes dreadful.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.480
We should have made a hot soup.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.650
Forget about that time.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.610
Having you with me is enough.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.660
You're shaking.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.080
Let me bear your darkness
and past with you.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.300
I'm your other half.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.720
I can't help but remember.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.060
Remember the man who killed my heart.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.100
The man I killed.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:39.780
You once told me that you
killed someone you loved.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.530
Yes. I loved him.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:48.910
But that's because I didn't know.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:53.370
He was a foe of York
and my father's killer:

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.330
the Lancastrian king!

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:02.590
I was young then. I found unease
and loneliness hard to bear.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:06.100
He was my salvation.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:09.970
He was innocent as a child my own age

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:14.060
and a grown man, warm as a father.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:19.820
But in the end... he couldn't love me.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.110
I thought my wounds were gone,

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:25.450
but the more fulfilled I am,
the wider they open.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:30.950
So I can't help thinking that one day

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.710
you'll do the same.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.000
Richard.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.250
Call to me.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.630
Say my name.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:44.930
Yes.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:50.100
Memories are merely timeworn corpses.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:52.930
Henry.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.020
Henry...

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.730
Why?

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:03.490
Why do I know this sound?

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.370
What? What?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.750
What's come over me?

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.000
It won't stop.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.960
When I pose as a shepherd
or feel the heat of blood

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:26.010
my dim existence seemed a little brighter.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:31.060
The Duke of Buckingham
asked you to save someone.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.810
His name is...

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.140
...George Plantagenet.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.600
King Edward's little brother.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:48.320
But perhaps, since before I was born,

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.240
I've always, always...

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.580
I too want to love someone.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.380
What?

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.590
I'll go look.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.010
Who--

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.680
Where have I seen this man before?

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.260
The Lancastrian king!

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:17.060
That's it. This is no mere resemblance.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.640
He looks identical!

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.360
Name yourself!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.230
The man who found me
called me James Tyrrell.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.440
James Tyrrell!

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.910
I've been watching all along.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:34.490
The way he opens his heart
to you is beautiful.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.960
I want to join you in that radiance.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:46.170
If you leave at once,
I promise to grant your wish later.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.720
If you understand, go!

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:01.810
Honestly. There's such a thing
as being <i>too</i> kind to commoners.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.730
You need to be stern with them.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.230
Royalty must--

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:08.240
B-By the way, Beth,
what brings you to the palace?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.650
I got an invitation.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:16.790
Uncle Richard must have realized that
I could safely join in a masquerade.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.960
What about Aunt Elizabeth?

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:23.460
She gave me permission,
if you can believe it.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:28.050
God has not yet forsaken us.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:31.880
I'll prepare a dress for you
somehow, so go in style.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:36.060
But I thought you couldn't
stand Uncle Richard.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:39.220
Your life is your own.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.900
A mother shares her daughter's happiness.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:51.240
Knowing my mother, I'm sure
she's scheming something.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.490
Even so...

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.200
...I wanted to see you all.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:04.170
But I should really leave
before I'm recognized.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:10.960
I want to dance more.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.260
Would you dance with us too?

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:17.680
Sure!

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.430
You went too far.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.560
When do you mean?

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.310
The play! Tonight! All of it!

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.770
Oh, but it was just so fun that--

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:32.070
You'll endanger my position if
you make yourself conspicuous!

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:36.070
But it seems we have
a full cast of actors now.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.410
Actors?

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:38.740
Yes.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:41.410
And a script ending in a checkmate.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:42.830
Dad.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.170
"Dad"?!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.580
What gives you the right to call me that?

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:52.090
Oh, please. We've known
the feel of the same hole.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:56.390
You're my wife's son, not mine!

00:08:56.390 --> 00:09:01.100
Leave me! I want no more
to do with rebels!

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:05.810
I suppose you wouldn't want
a rebel to call you "dad."

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:09.980
But how will you feel once I'm king?

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.400
What do you mean?!

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.070
Well then, "Father," farewell.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.910
See you in the palace.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.540
I brought you clothes.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:24.660
Allow me.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.550
And now the night is over.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.630
We're a king and a duke again.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.350
Yes, Your Royal Majesty.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.100
Henry!

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:57.660
Ugh. I wish the party would never end.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:01.280
Don't be silly. It <i>was</i> fun, though.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.910
Who do you think that beautiful lady was?

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:09.210
Did you see the child dressed as a cat?

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.840
A charming little boy?

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.800
I danced with him!

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.840
Oh? You saw his face, then.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:21.100
That was His Majesty's only son, Edward.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.850
I think he did look like the queen!

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:28.980
No one recognizes him because
he hasn't been to London much.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.230
His Majesty probably wanted to hide him.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:33.230
After all,

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.940
the boy looks nothing like the king.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.530
Ow.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.950
I'm so sorry.

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.540
Prince Edward?

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:50.500
I hear that my father loved to fight.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.880
I'm no good at it.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.260
I'd rather study.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:02.180
Troubled times forced him to take up arms.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.970
Is something worrying you?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:09.850
I was told that I look
nothing like my father.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:14.360
That I'm not his son.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:16.530
Edward.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.740
Father.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:22.570
Tell me about it.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:28.000
The first time was at the banquet.
I was only startled then.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.620
But the next morning...

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:33.500
It's true. Just look at his hair.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.670
I sense no royal blood in him.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.460
So, a cuckoo's child caused
their estrangement.

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:43.760
Everyone whispered strange
things when they saw me.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.600
They've never been an affectionate couple.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.470
Is that all?

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:51.060
Don't you all remember that rumor?

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:53.900
"Demon."

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.230
They called you a demon, Father.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:02.240
I couldn't argue back.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.370
I hated it,

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.660
but I was too frightened to speak.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:10.330
I'm a weakling, so I need to get stronger.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:15.130
For a moment, I imagined

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:19.250
this child turning his back
on me like my mother did.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.840
What a pretty garden.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:31.680
When I was your age,
I never once admired a flower.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:34.310
The white rose was an oath of vengeance.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:38.150
The red rose was proof of shed blood.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:41.570
But now they all seem beautiful.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:46.780
I needn't seek meaning in them;
they're simply there.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:53.910
Before I knew it, I found them dear to me.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:02.840
I didn't resemble my father either.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:07.390
But no one shared a stronger
bond than we did.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:12.930
Is this feeling truly hypocrisy or pity?

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:17.480
Gorgeous, dashing, and kind.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.480
Father!

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:23.610
You are my light!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:27.240
I may not know the true nature of love,

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:30.660
but I'm certain that I feel it now.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.710
Edward, my son.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:38.630
By your mere presence, you...

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:46.010
Buckingham, I trust you realize
why I summoned you.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:50.850
Yes. The absurd rumors running
rampant in the palace.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:56.060
No matter how often I suppress them,
they return like cursed ghosts.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.350
These rumors are fatal to a king.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:01.480
Edward is shaken as well.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:07.530
I sense intent behind
these rumors' spread.

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:11.200
I'll take measures at once,
and so should Your Majesty.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.200
Such as?

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:16.830
Even if we find the culprit,
the threat will return

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.880
until we cut it off at the source.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:24.590
The best way to dispel
these untoward rumors

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:29.510
is for the queen to bear
you a child at once.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:30.640
That isn't...

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.520
Your Majesty, I speak
as your loyal retainer.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:39.190
But what if she rejects me?

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.860
Rejects this body of mine?

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:46.530
Unthinkable. She knows her duty as queen.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:49.200
--She must realize--
--She doesn't know.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.490
She doesn't know me.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.120
What about you?

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.080
Everything.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.460
What do you mean?

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:04.380
I've never made love to her.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.630
Edward isn't my son by blood.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.970
You swore

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:15.350
to keep no secrets.

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:16.470
Buckingham.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.930
Disinherit him.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:24.730
Have you forgotten that we
condemned Edward V as illegitimate?

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.570
If he is not of your blood, you must--

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.030
His blood is royal.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.910
His father was King Henry's son.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.780
The Lancastrian prince?!

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:37.370
He's not your son <i>and</i> of
our enemies' bloodline?!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.000
Even your brother's sons would be better!

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.880
This is no distant memory!

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:46.250
You must see what a
threat this secret poses

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:48.920
to King Richard III!

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:55.180
I will protect Edward.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:58.930
That child is my son.

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:03.730
I always had suspicions...

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:09.780
...but I trusted you.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:13.070
Henry.

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:17.080
Why? Why?

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:20.120
The child of King Henry's son?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:23.670
Don't give in to emotion.
Think what you ought to do.

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:25.920
There must be a solution.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.470
I've been waiting, Henry.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.840
Why here, of all places?

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.350
I have no time to indulge you now.

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:37.260
Begone!

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.770
No. You promised me.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.100
Return to where you belong!

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:45.310
No. I won't leave until you tell me.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:48.020
How can I love people?

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:52.240
Like you love that person
and that person loves you.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:57.070
Why would you want to know love?

00:16:57.070 --> 00:17:00.620
Once you do, you can never go back.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:04.160
I thought I need only
cut a path through briars.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:07.130
I feared nothing then, but no more.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:12.050
My feelings distract me
even at this moment.

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:16.680
Why? Why?

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:19.260
What did I give up on you for?

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:23.310
Explain yourself!

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:25.440
You looked sad.

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:28.400
Don't treat me like a weakling!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.610
But I want to save miserable people.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.740
The strong don't seek my salvation.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:38.490
That's right. I don't need you!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.620
But what of Richard?

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:45.370
Richard said he'd protect
the Lancastrian boy.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:47.420
The blood of Henry VI!

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:53.090
Edward's sons would be better, he says?

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:54.840
Why?

00:17:54.840 --> 00:18:00.430
We swore to shoulder my darkness and
past together. To be halves of one whole.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.730
What if...

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:10.360
What if he never returns?

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:14.150
What if I've lost him?

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.450
That's impossible.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.490
Calm down.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.910
We can resolve a trifle
like this soon enough.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.750
He only left to take measures.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:27.210
Yes. He's my other half.

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:28.500
He'll soon be--

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:29.920
Buckingham!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.300
It's me, Richard.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:34.250
Anne.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:39.640
My lady's maids asked to see
acrobatics at tonight's dinner.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.720
May I call for jesters?

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.810
Yes. I don't mind.

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:47.690
Richard, you look ill.

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:51.480
I lost sight of you partway
through the banquet,

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:53.730
but I see you partied through the night.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:19:00.240
You were truly beautiful that night.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:04.160
Richard, let me see to
the dinner arrangements.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.000
I'm sure that Edward
will like jesters too.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:14.420
I meant to ask him

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:17.380
who the devil that abducted
the beauty was.

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:23.100
But that look on Richard's face...

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:27.890
What am I doing?
I can't let this shake me.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:31.730
I have everything I wished for right here.

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:41.660
Catesby, where's Buckingham?

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:45.780
He will be dining with a guest
in his chambers tonight.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.160
I see.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:52.880
Father, may I ask you for something?

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.750
Yes. What?

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:58.210
I'd like you to bring Beth
back to the palace.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:01.220
Disinherit him.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:07.510
She seemed so happy dancing
with everyone at the party.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:10.230
He wants me to abandon this child?

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:12.190
Absurd.

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.980
There must be another way.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.730
No matter how many briars bar my path.

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:22.280
That's right. You even made
this crown worthwhile.

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:26.830
Familiar unease and fear
crawled up from the darkness,

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:31.960
forming a dark pool in my heart
no matter how I tried to stop it.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.580
Father?

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.540
Do as you please.

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.130
Do you mean it?

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.210
Richard?

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:40.590
Don't mind me. I'll be right back.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:49.640
Where are you? Hurry to my side,

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:50.680
Henry!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:02.320
Jesters and more food than they can eat!

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.530
It must be nice to be king!

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:07.870
And the former king sits
reading in an animal pen.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:11.950
Be quiet and dream of Mom,
you illiterate baby.

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:16.250
"I miss you, Mommy!
Take me away from here!"

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.170
I only said that once! In my sleep!

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.170
Stop harping on about it!

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:24.800
He's useless! He was just born sooner!

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:27.220
Being stuck in here with him is hell.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:31.310
Really, when will we be
able to leave this place?

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:34.770
Richard had better not
leave us here forever.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.690
Your Majesty,

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.940
King Edward V.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:46.820
Have no fear.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.700
I've come to save you.
